# This controls which ECPay API (stage/sandbox vs real-money production)
# the backend talks to — see functions/src/ecpayClient.ts. Unlike PayPal,
# ECPay's frontend checkout has no separate client-id to keep in sync (see
# src/ecpayCheckout.ts): the whole signed request is server-built, so this
# is the only place the environment choice lives. Defaults to "stage" if
# unset (ecpayClient.ts's ECPAY_ENV default), matching the safe-by-default
# pattern PAYPAL_ENV used to follow on the main branch.
#
# "stage" uses ECPay's publicly documented test merchant (MerchantID
# 2000132) — safe for development, no real charges. Set to "production"
# only once ECPAY_MERCHANT_ID/ECPAY_HASH_KEY/ECPAY_HASH_IV in Firebase
# Secret Manager hold a real approved 特約商店 account's credentials.
ECPAY_ENV=stage
